\section{The player punting and return blocks}{


The two player endpoints carry a 15-column punting block, prefixed \code{punting_}
(e.g. \code{punting_net_yards_per_punt}), and a 10-column punt return block,
prefixed \code{returning_}. A player who only punted has \code{NA} return columns, and
the reverse.

The punting block:\tabular{lll}{
   col_name \tab type \tab description \cr
   punts \tab integer \tab Punts. \cr
   punt_yards_available \tab integer \tab Punts with known gross yards (the denominator for \code{yards_per_punt}). \cr
   punt_yards \tab integer \tab Gross punt yards over those punts. \cr
   yards_per_punt \tab double \tab Gross yards per punt. \cr
   longest_punt \tab integer \tab Longest punt, in gross yards. \cr
   punts50plus \tab integer \tab Punts of 50 or more gross yards. \cr
   net_punt_yards_available \tab integer \tab Punts with known net yards (the denominator for \code{net_yards_per_punt}). \cr
   net_punt_yards \tab integer \tab Net punt yards over those punts: gross yards minus return yards, less 20 for a touchback. \cr
   net_yards_per_punt \tab double \tab Net yards per punt. \cr
   touchbacks \tab integer \tab Punts that ended in a touchback. \cr
   fair_catches \tab integer \tab Punts fair caught. \cr
   out_of_bounds \tab integer \tab Punts that went out of bounds. \cr
   downed \tab integer \tab Punts downed by the kicking team. \cr
   inside20 \tab integer \tab Punts after which the receiving team took possession inside its own 20, excluding touchbacks. \cr
   blocked \tab integer \tab Punts blocked. \cr
}


The return block:\tabular{lll}{
   col_name \tab type \tab description \cr
   returns \tab integer \tab Punt returns. \cr
